From: Stephen Ross <s.ross@cep-claddings.example> (CEP Claddings Ltd)
To: k.gundersen@steni.example
Date: 2003-07-24
Subject: Aberfeldy project - problems with Steni Colour panels

Mr Gundersen,

We are encountering problems on the Aberfeldy project. Joyners, the cladding subcontractor, wrote to us on 14 July 2003 to say that our outstanding invoices would not be paid as the Steni Colour panels supplied were "not fit for use" due to poor scratch resistance, and on 21 July 2003 said they would not pay our outstanding account until all issues in relation to the project were resolved. Countryside, the main contractor, says some of the boards have been fixed and found not to be acceptable, and that we must make a sensible offer in relation to the board not used.

Samples were sent to Steni Norden in Norway on 15 July for scratch resistance testing.

Consequently, the sum that is being withheld from us by Joyners will in turn be withheld from Steni Norden.

Stephen Ross
CEP Claddings Ltd

